{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '668,680p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\"","aggregated_output":"This flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\nviews are durable or rebuildable from durable entries. Reads use cursor\npagination with default limits:\n\n- archive entries: default 100, max 200\n- turns: default 50, max 100\n- derived views: default 50\n\nA derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\nreturn degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\navailable.\n\n## Implementation Chunks\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 3-5 are coherent once canonical archive rows already exist: archive reads, turn derivation, and derived views share stable IDs and degradation semantics.\",\"The seam between Story 2 finalization and Story 1 persistence is where the epic breaks: live execution output is still funneled through legacy `processHistoryItems`, so later stories rely on archive row shapes that the shipped runtime cannot actually produce.\",\"Story 6 provenance enrichment and Story 5 tool-aware turn/view behavior are both validated mostly against hand-seeded archive rows rather than rows emitted by the real completion hooks.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The Convex storage layer matches the tech design, but the control-plane finalization boundary never moved up to finalized runtime objects; it is still coupled to presentation-oriented `ProcessHistoryItem` records.\",\"Read-time enrichment is correctly separated from canonical truth, but no upstream writer populates the related artifact/source IDs that the enrichment layer consumes.\",\"Derived turns and derived views remain rebuildable projections and do not mutate archive truth; the main architectural drift is at capture time, not projection time.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Both requested gates passed on May 5, 2026: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all`.\",\"Coverage is strong for storage, ordering, pagination, turn grouping, derived-view refresh, and degraded-read behavior once archive rows already exist.\",\"Coverage is weak on end-to-end emission: tests create `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and provenance-bearing archive rows directly in fixtures/service stores instead of proving that the live runtime can emit them.\",\"`verify-all` still ends with a scaffold-only `test:e2e` step, so no browser-level end-to-end archive flow currently executes.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The default runtime path is still the shared placeholder execution payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts`, and that payload emits a synthetic `process_event` plus placeholder side-work text instead of a real process-type model/tool/runtime flow.\",\"Production archive append is currently limited to accepted user responses and legacy history-item bridging; there is no real append path for `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` entries.\",\"Artifact/source provenance enrichment is real on read, but no live writer currently persists the related artifact-version or source-provenance IDs that the read path expects.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"archive-taxonomy-production-gap\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"The shipped archive pipeline cannot emit four of the seven required canonical entry kinds\",\"evidence\":\"`ExecutionResult` only carries legacy `ProcessHistoryItem[]` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts`), `processHistoryItemKindSchema` only allows `user_message`, `process_message`, `progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and `process_event` (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts`), and the archive compatibility bridge maps only `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into canonical rows (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts`). `ProcessEnvironmentService` archives runtime output only through that bridge (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts`), so the live system has no real append path for `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"archive-provenance-write-gap\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Live archive writes never attach artifact-version or source-provenance references\",\"evidence\":\"The read path is built to enrich `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts`), but the shipped producers hard-code both fields to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts`, `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts`). The only execution-bridge payload is `ProcessHistoryItem`, which exposes `relatedArtifactId` but no artifact-version or source-provenance field (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts`), so real archive rows cannot satisfy provenance visibility requirements. The passing provenance tests seed those IDs directly in fixtures and test stores (`tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`, `tests/fixtures/archive.ts`) instead of proving a live producer can emit them.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts\",\"tests/fixtures/archive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"placeholder-execution-production-path\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"The default execution lane is still a placeholder path\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts` still builds the repo-wide \\\"default execution payload,\\\" writes a \\\"Default Execution Summary,\\\" and reports \\\"Execution placeholder completed...\\\" while emitting only a single `process_event`. That is a material non-real production path for this epic because the archive is being exercised primarily against placeholder runtime output rather than real process-type execution.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"A new finalized runtime-object contract is still needed if the archive is supposed to capture `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, and `tool_result` without collapsing back to presentation history rows.\",\"The implementation still needs a concrete producer for `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId` during finalization; the current codebase only implements the read-side enrichment.\",\"No executable end-to-end archive/browser suite currently runs because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only in the epic gate.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
